# Design System Tokens

All color and typography values in CSS, SCSS, and Tailwind must use design-system tokens defined in `src/styles/tokens.css` and `src/styles/globals.css`. Never hard-code values when a token exists.

## Color: use `--ds-*` tokens, not mapped aliases

`globals.css` defines shorthand aliases (`--foreground`, `--background`, `--card`, etc.) that map to `--ds-*` tokens. **Do not use the aliases in component styles.** Use the `--ds-*` tokens directly so the intent is explicit and grep-able.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — mapped alias hides the actual DS role */
color: var(--foreground);
background: var(--background);
background: var(--card);
color: var(--muted-foreground);
border-color: var(--border);
background: var(--sidebar);
background: var(--accent);
background: var(--destructive);

/* ✅ GOOD — DS token is explicit */
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-neutral-primary);
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-quaternary);
border-color: var(--ds-borders-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-brand-teal-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-error-primary);
```

### Alias → DS token mapping (quick reference)

| Alias | DS Token |
|---|---|
| `--foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--background` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` |
| `--card` / `--card-foreground` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` / `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--popover` / `--popover-foreground` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` / `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--primary` | `--ds-background-brand-purple-primary` |
| `--primary-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed` |
| `--secondary` | `--ds-background-neutral-secondary` |
| `--secondary-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--muted` | `--ds-background-neutral-quaternary` |
| `--muted-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-quaternary` |
| `--accent` | `--ds-background-brand-teal-primary` |
| `--accent-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed` |
| `--destructive` | `--ds-background-error-primary` |
| `--destructive-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed` |
| `--border` | `--ds-borders-neutral-primary` |
| `--input` / `--input-background` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` |
| `--ring` | `--ds-borders-brand-teal-primary` |
| `--sidebar` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` |
| `--sidebar-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |

## Color: no hardcoded hex values

Never write raw hex like `#fff`, `#292F36`, `#69788a`, etc. Pick the matching `--ds-*` token.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
color: #fff;
color: #292F36;

/* ✅ GOOD */
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed);
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-black-fixed);
```

## Typography: use size tokens

Available font-size tokens (from `globals.css`):

| Token | Value |
|---|---|
| `--text-h1` | 48px |
| `--text-h2` | 34px |
| `--text-h3` | 28px |
| `--text-h4` | 24px |
| `--text-base` | 16px |
| `--text-label` | 12px |

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
font-size: 12px;
font-size: 16px;
font-size: 24px;

/* ✅ GOOD */
font-size: var(--text-label);
font-size: var(--text-base);
font-size: var(--text-h4);
```

If a design truly requires a size not in this table (e.g. 14px, 20px), add a new token to `globals.css` (e.g. `--text-sm: 14px`) rather than hard-coding the value.

## Typography: use weight and family tokens

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
font-weight: 600;
font-family: 'Figtree', sans-serif;

/* ✅ GOOD */
font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
font-family: var(--font-body);
```

Available weight tokens: `--font-weight-semibold` (600), `--font-weight-medium` (500), `--font-weight-normal` (400).
Available family tokens: `--font-heading` (Barlow Semi Condensed), `--font-body` (Figtree), `--font-mono` (Google Sans Code).

## SCSS files

The SCSS token file `src/styles/_tokens.scss` and mixins in `src/styles/_mixins.scss` also contain mapped aliases. When writing new SCSS, prefer `var(--ds-*)` over the SCSS `$color-*` variables for the same reasons above.

## When to use mapped aliases

The **only** place mapped aliases belong is in `globals.css` itself (where they are defined) and in Tailwind utility classes (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`) which rely on the `@theme` block. In hand-written CSS/SCSS, always use the `--ds-*` form.
